### Tested versions

The code described is the current master branch, `core/object/object.cpp`

### System information

Linux 7.0 (Ubuntu), Godot 4.6.stable custom editor build (target=editor debug_symbols=yes) with the godot_voxel module, AMD RX 9070 / RADV. The problem is code-level and platform independent.

### Issue description

**How this was found** is described at length in the closed [#122291](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122291).

The function `_gdvirtual_init_method_ptr` is called simultaneously by multiple threads, so the following part should be thread-safe:

```cpp
#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED
	if (_extension->reloadable) {
		VirtualMethodTracker *tracker = memnew(VirtualMethodTracker);
		tracker->method = (void **)&r_fn_ptr;
		tracker->next = virtual_method_list;
		virtual_method_list = tracker;
	}
#endif
```
As suggested in [#122291](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122291#issuecomment-5259075675) the least intrusive solution is:

```cpp
#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED
	if (_extension->reloadable) {
		static Mutex gdvirtual_init_mutex;
		MutexLock lock(gdvirtual_init_mutex);
		VirtualMethodTracker *tracker = memnew(VirtualMethodTracker);
		tracker->method = (void **)&r_fn_ptr;
		tracker->next = virtual_method_list;
		virtual_method_list = tracker;
	}
#endif
```

What I can't answer is if there must be a more global protection on file level for the freeing of the list because I don't know if `_gdvirtual_init_method_ptr` and `Object::clear_internal_extension()` can be called at the same time. Snippet of `Object::clear_internal_extension()`:

```cpp
	while (virtual_method_list) {
		(*virtual_method_list->method) = nullptr;
		virtual_method_list = virtual_method_list->next;
	}
```

**What this doesn't fix:** the guard around the call to `_gdvirtual_init_method_ptr`, in the macro generated by `make_virtuals.py` also has a race condition, but the worst thing that can happen is that there are duplicate entries. With the mutex the list itself stays consistent.

